<title>UK: Railtrack up but Warburg restates &quot;sell&quot;.</title>
<headline>Railtrack up but Warburg restates &quot;sell&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Railtrack Plc were boosted by a rising market on Tuesday despite a restatement of a &quot;sell&quot; recommendation by analysts at SBC Warburg, traders said.</p>
<p>Railtrack shares were three pence higher at 397 by 1330 GMT having been as low as 390p earlier.</p>
<p>Market sources said Warburg considered Railtrack shares to be overvalued and had reiterated a &quot;sell&quot; recommendation first issued last month.</p>
<p>&quot;There was a bit of selling early on but they're doing better now,&quot; one market-maker said.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Mashall, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
